[sliver] The strip reading measures the 0.75 mm projection of each functional J1/J2 retaining lip, not the hook's material thickness. Each lip has 3 mm stock behind its flat underside and spans the bank's full 16 mm cable width. The 2.2 mm seat depth, 0.75 mm lip and 45-degree entry use the accepted cable-hook section. The two lips retain the front-going leads in the separate J1 and J2 cavities; the seven-lead J1 grouping retains its stated physical-fit scope.
alternatives: Removing the projection opens the retaining mouth to the full seat depth and removes the selected capture. Filling below it occupies the cable cavity. Thickening the projection into that cavity changes the accepted entry and retention section. This finding conflates the functional lip's reach with a thin structural wall.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=131.200 y=74.825 z=21.700
click: x=131.200 y=80.025 z=16.150

[ledge] Functional flat retaining undersides of the J1/J2 cable hooks. Each 12 mm2 face is the 0.75 mm projection across the 16 mm cable span, backed by 3 mm hook stock. Its flat underside catches the leads beneath the 45-degree entry. The 2.2 mm seat depth, lip and entry follow the accepted cable-hook section; the installed seven-lead J1 grouping has its own physical-fit scope. Tree(auto)/Default supplies the current native support decisions.
alternatives: Removing or sloping the retaining underside changes the selected cable capture; filling beneath it closes the cable seat. The overhang is the named retaining interface, rather than a cut remnant between unrelated features.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=128.533 y=74.700 z=21.700
click: x=128.533 y=79.900 z=16.150

[thin] Specific B-fill channel-cover section: the 6.8 mm guide and its 0.25 mm supported-roof allowance leave 2.20 mm of retaining roof beneath the Z253.4 lid face. Three recessed M3x10 screws clamp this cover to the full-height cup block on both sides of the bend. This is the named channel cover, rather than an ordinary standing wall. The production-source receipt in foam-cap/b-fill-channel-review/native-review.json records its roof, clamps and 1.60 mm gap to the original PCB. The fit reading does not establish a measured load rating.
alternatives: Raising this roof to obtain 3 mm stock spends 0.8 mm of the 1.60 mm PCB-tail gap. Lowering the channel changes its selected fore entry and the bend's intersection with the cup floor and reservoir grip. The specific cover section retains the reviewed channel and component datums.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
