[thin] Specific 4 mm flavor-line flexures: these four free jaws use the C2 profile scaled from the 6.35 mm section to the 4 mm bore, giving a 1.52 mm working jaw. Their mouths permit direct press-in insertion; the filled roots retain 3 mm stock. The smaller section is a defined spring, with no transferred claim about measured force or fatigue.
alternatives: A 3 mm jaw changes the spring section and mouth compliance. Filling above the tube equator closes the loading mouth; a rigid saddle with a separate closure adds a part and an assembly step.
