[thin] Retained leaning-line entry at native X−134.5/Y−32.5: the Ø7.5 mm conduit opens through the outer 2 mm of the lid as a 38-degree countersink. The ranked 2.28–2.49 mm section is between this conical tube-bearing mouth and the fixed casing edge. It is the entry profile for the leaning line.
alternatives: A 3 mm rim requires moving the conduit inward or narrowing the countersink. The first moves its cup column and installed route; the second reduces the specified 38-degree tube-exit allowance.
